From 4ff07f87fb48a1cd57c1be88aa2cd7d92e969504 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 02:44:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] generic-parallel behaviours: common contract with the
 material properties

- the batch functions (integration, initialize functions, post-processings,
  rotations, standalone models) are named after the functions of the
  `generic` interface followed by `_generic_parallel`; the name of a
  behaviour or of a model can't contain `_generic_parallel`;
- version 3 of the data structures (`MFRONT_GPB_API_VERSION`):
  `mfront_gpb_Statistics` has the members of `mfront_gpmp_Statistics`
  (opaque keys of the first failure and of the first unreliable result,
  `MFront/GenericParallel/StatisticsKeys.hxx`) followed by `rdt`; the
  output status gives the index of the first unreliable result; `statuses`
  is placed after `s1` in the batch data; types of the pointers to the
  generated functions;
- `<name>_generic_parallel_report`, exported by each library, analyses the
  statistics of asynchronous computations (`mfront_gpb_report`,
  `mfront_gpb_getStatus` removed); `mfront_gpb_initializeStatistics` takes
  the time step scaling factor of the batch;
- errors of the batch: `-5` invalid arguments (a null output status
  included), `-6` invalid parameters (parameters file which can't be read),
  `-7` runtime error of the backend, as for the material properties;
- tests: report function, index of the first unreliable result, invalid
  parameters files of a behaviour and of a behaviour variable, refused
  names of a behaviour and of a model; documentation and release notes.
